1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,040
Banana and pineapple flavourings often get their smell

2
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:04,160
from esters.

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:07,360
Pentyl ethanoate is usually described as smelling like

4
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:10,960
banana, and ethyl butanoate like pineapple.

5
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:12,960
Each one can be made from two smaller

6
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:16,000
molecules: a carboxylic acid, like the ones in

7
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:18,640
the last video, and an alcohol.

8
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:21,040
So how do the two halves join?

9
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:23,920
Why does the reaction never quite finish?

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,680
And how do you get the ester out?

11
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:30,220
Take ethanoic acid and ethanol.

12
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:32,580
The acid loses the O H from its

13
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:35,620
carboxyl group, and the alcohol loses the H

14
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:36,860
from its O H.

15
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:39,460
Together, those make water.

16
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:42,260
The two parts link through the alcohol's oxygen,

17
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:44,420
giving ethyl ethanoate.

18
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:47,140
This new link, a C double bond O,

19
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:49,620
then an oxygen, then a carbon chain, is

20
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:51,220
the ester group.

21
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:53,620
When two molecules join and release a small

22
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:57,540
molecule like water, it's called a condensation reaction.

23
00:00:59,567 --> 00:01:02,206
Ester names have two words, one for each

24
00:01:02,287 --> 00:01:02,766
half.

25
00:01:03,247 --> 00:01:05,766
The alcohol part comes first, named like a

26
00:01:05,807 --> 00:01:08,446
branch: ethanol gives ethyl.

27
00:01:09,007 --> 00:01:12,046
The acid part comes second, ending in oate,

28
00:01:12,127 --> 00:01:13,806
just like the salt in the last video.

29
00:01:14,367 --> 00:01:16,526
Ethanoic acid gives ethanoate.

30
00:01:17,007 --> 00:01:19,006
So this is ethyl ethanoate.

31
00:01:19,647 --> 00:01:23,646
Careful: formulas are usually written acid side first,

32
00:01:23,687 --> 00:01:26,206
but the name puts the alcohol part first.

33
00:01:26,447 --> 00:01:27,646
The order matters.

34
00:01:28,207 --> 00:01:31,486
Ethyl butanoate and butyl ethanoate have the same

35
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:33,966
formula, but they're different molecules.

36
00:01:35,967 --> 00:01:38,886
Exam questions often go the other way: here's

37
00:01:38,927 --> 00:01:40,726
an ester, what made it?

38
00:01:41,007 --> 00:01:43,086
Find the C double bond O, and cut

39
00:01:43,127 --> 00:01:45,166
at the single-bonded oxygen next to it.

40
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:47,486
The side with the C double bond O

41
00:01:47,567 --> 00:01:48,686
came from the acid.

42
00:01:49,167 --> 00:01:51,486
The oxygen, and the chain beyond it, came

43
00:01:51,567 --> 00:01:52,366
from the alcohol.

44
00:01:52,927 --> 00:01:55,006
In C H three C H two C

45
00:01:55,167 --> 00:01:57,726
O O C H three, the acid side

46
00:01:57,807 --> 00:02:01,206
has three carbons, so it's propanoic acid.

47
00:02:01,487 --> 00:02:03,966
The alcohol side has one carbon, so it's

48
00:02:04,047 --> 00:02:04,686
methanol.

49
00:02:05,167 --> 00:02:07,326
That makes it methyl propanoate.

50
00:02:09,334 --> 00:02:11,653
An ester has no O H.

51
00:02:11,894 --> 00:02:14,293
So its molecules can't hydrogen bond to each

52
00:02:14,414 --> 00:02:17,573
other, just dipole-dipole and dispersion forces.

53
00:02:18,294 --> 00:02:21,493
Compare three molecules of almost the same mass,

54
00:02:21,574 --> 00:02:22,213
eighty eight.

55
00:02:22,774 --> 00:02:26,133
Ethyl ethanoate boils at about seventy seven degrees,

56
00:02:26,214 --> 00:02:29,013
pentan-one-ol at one hundred and thirty eight, and

57
00:02:29,094 --> 00:02:32,293
butanoic acid at one hundred and sixty four.

58
00:02:32,334 --> 00:02:35,333
So small esters evaporate easily, and their smell

59
00:02:35,414 --> 00:02:36,653
reaches your nose.

60
00:02:36,934 --> 00:02:40,373
And notice: ethyl ethanoate and butanoic acid are

61
00:02:40,574 --> 00:02:43,253
both C four H eight O two.

62
00:02:43,414 --> 00:02:46,533
Only the acid fizzes with sodium hydrogen carbonate.

63
00:02:48,534 --> 00:02:51,813
At room temperature, this reaction is very slow.

64
00:02:52,294 --> 00:02:54,533
So we add a few drops of concentrated

65
00:02:54,614 --> 00:02:57,213
sulfuric acid as a catalyst, and heat the

66
00:02:57,254 --> 00:02:58,933
mixture under reflux.

67
00:02:59,254 --> 00:03:01,813
As in the ethanol video, the condenser cools

68
00:03:01,894 --> 00:03:05,333
the vapours, so volatile ethanol and ethyl ethanoate

69
00:03:05,414 --> 00:03:07,453
drip back instead of escaping.

70
00:03:07,734 --> 00:03:11,173
Concentrated sulfuric acid is corrosive, and these liquids

71
00:03:11,254 --> 00:03:13,893
are flammable, so heat with an electric heater

72
00:03:13,974 --> 00:03:16,533
or a water bath, never a flame.

73
00:03:18,534 --> 00:03:21,053
But esterification is reversible.

74
00:03:21,334 --> 00:03:23,333
Water can split the ester back into the

75
00:03:23,414 --> 00:03:24,813
acid and alcohol.

76
00:03:25,094 --> 00:03:27,893
So the mixture reaches equilibrium, with all four

77
00:03:27,974 --> 00:03:29,653
substances still there.

78
00:03:29,974 --> 00:03:32,373
Start with equal amounts of ethanoic acid and

79
00:03:32,454 --> 00:03:35,253
ethanol, and only about two thirds turns into

80
00:03:35,454 --> 00:03:35,733
ester.

81
00:03:36,214 --> 00:03:39,093
That's why the equation needs the equilibrium arrow,

82
00:03:39,174 --> 00:03:40,293
not a single arrow.

83
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:45,020
To get more, use Le Chatelier's principle from

84
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:46,220
Module five.

85
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:49,020
Add an excess of one reactant, often the

86
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:49,740
cheaper one.

87
00:03:50,220 --> 00:03:52,060
The system shifts to use up some of

88
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:53,660
it, and makes more ester.

89
00:03:54,220 --> 00:03:56,860
With three times as much ethanol, about nine

90
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:58,860
tenths of the acid becomes ester.

91
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:02,700
Removing water helps too, and the concentrated sulfuric

92
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:03,980
acid takes up a little.

93
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:06,700
But the catalyst doesn't change the yield.

94
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:10,140
It speeds up both directions, so equilibrium just

95
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:11,180
arrives sooner.

96
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:16,640
After reflux, the flask holds the ester, leftover

97
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:20,240
acid and alcohol, water, and sulfuric acid.

98
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:23,120
Pour it into a separating funnel with water.

99
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:25,680
Most of the ethanol and the sulfuric acid

100
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:28,320
dissolve in the water, but the ester doesn't

101
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:31,040
mix well, so it forms its own layer.

102
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:33,520
Wash it with sodium carbonate solution.

103
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:36,560
The leftover acid becomes a salt that dissolves

104
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:39,360
in the water layer, and carbon dioxide forms,

105
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:41,560
so the funnel is vented often.

106
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:44,480
Then separate the layers, dry the ester, and

107
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:47,360
distil it, collecting what boils near seventy seven

108
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:48,080
degrees.

109
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:51,200
Ethanol boils at seventy eight, so that's only

110
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:52,160
a rough check.

111
00:04:54,167 --> 00:04:56,726
You can even make ethyl ethanoate from ethanol

112
00:04:56,887 --> 00:04:57,646
alone.

113
00:04:57,927 --> 00:05:01,926
First, oxidise some ethanol with acidified dichromate under

114
00:05:02,007 --> 00:05:04,086
reflux, to make ethanoic acid.

115
00:05:04,727 --> 00:05:07,526
Then react that acid with more ethanol, with

116
00:05:07,607 --> 00:05:10,766
concentrated sulfuric acid, under reflux.

117
00:05:11,207 --> 00:05:13,366
In a flow chart, each box holds a

118
00:05:13,647 --> 00:05:16,326
