123
00:05:26,527 --> 00:05:29,366
Only a primary alcohol oxidises to an acid.

124
00:05:31,367 --> 00:05:35,286
So, acid plus alcohol, in equilibrium with ester

125
00:05:35,447 --> 00:05:36,486
plus water.

126
00:05:36,807 --> 00:05:39,446
In the name, the alcohol part comes first

127
00:05:39,527 --> 00:05:41,846
and ends in yl, and the acid part

128
00:05:41,927 --> 00:05:43,926
comes second and ends in oate.

129
00:05:44,567 --> 00:05:48,486
Excess reactant, or removing water, raises the yield.

130
00:05:48,887 --> 00:05:51,366
The catalyst makes it faster, not more.

131
00:05:51,927 --> 00:05:54,966
Heat speeds it too, and with reflux, nothing

132
00:05:55,047 --> 00:05:55,846
